      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\ud83d\udcda KEY DOCKER TERMS FOR BEGINNERS",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\ud83d\udcda KEY DOCKER TERMS FOR BEGINNERS",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.3
    },
    {
      "id": "DykDwifHju5KnWliGkbGE",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -630,
      "y": 290,
      "width": 417.59999999999997,
      "height": 358.8,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 784506854,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 502911509,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1780139500000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\ud83d\udcc4 DOCKERFILE\nA text file with a step-by-step recipe to build a\ncontainer image. It defines base OS, tools & code.\n\n\ud83d\udcbf IMAGE\nAn immutable (read-only) static package containing\neverything needed to run the app. Like a frozen cake.\n\n\ud83d\udce6 CONTAINER\nA running, live instance of an image. It is fully isolated\nfrom other containers and runs instantly. Like a baked cake.\n\n\ud83d\udcda REGISTRY (DOCKER HUB)\nA public/private cloud library where developers push\nand pull container images. Like an App Store.\n\n\ud83d\udcbe VOLUME\nA persistent hard-drive directory on the host system to\nstore databases and files so data is not lost on crash.\n\n\ud83c\udf10 NETWORK\nPrivate software-defined channels allowing containers\nto talk securely using service name DNS hostnames.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\ud83d\udcc4 DOCKERFILE\nA text file with a step-by-step recipe to build a\ncontainer image. It defines base OS, tools & code.\n\n\ud83d\udcbf IMAGE\nAn immutable (read-only) static package containing\neverything needed to run the app. Like a frozen cake.\n\n\ud83d\udce6 CONTAINER\nA running, live instance of an image. It is fully isolated\nfrom other containers and runs instantly. Like a baked cake.\n\n\ud83d\udcda REGISTRY (DOCKER HUB)\nA public/private cloud library where developers push\nand pull container images. Like an App Store.\n\n\ud83d\udcbe VOLUME\nA persistent hard-drive directory on the host system to\nstore databases and files so data is not lost on crash.\n\n\ud83c\udf10 NETWORK\nPrivate software-defined channels allowing containers\nto talk securely using service name DNS hostnames.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.3
    },
