      "text": "\ud83d\udee0\ufe0f 1. BUILD COMMANDS (Image Creation)",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\ud83d\udee0\ufe0f 1. BUILD COMMANDS (Image Creation)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.3
    },
    {
      "id": "lOQjl10qeGVYdlWyHXQ08",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -600,
      "y": 995,
      "width": 370.04,
      "height": 243.1,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1672444507,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 631218181,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1780139500000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "docker build -t name:tag .\n\ud83d\udc49 Build a container image from a Dockerfile.\n\ndocker build --no-cache -t name:tag .\n\ud83d\udc49 Forces rebuild of image layers, bypassing cache.\n\ndocker images\n\ud83d\udc49 List all container images stored locally on your system.\n\ndocker rmi image_id\n\ud83d\udc49 Deletes a local image to free disk space.\n\ndocker tag source_tag target_tag\n\ud83d\udc49 Creates an alias tag referencing a target image.\n\ndocker history image_name\n\ud83d\udc49 Shows the list of filesystem layers in an image.",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "docker build -t name:tag .\n\ud83d\udc49 Build a container image from a Dockerfile.\n\ndocker build --no-cache -t name:tag .\n\ud83d\udc49 Forces rebuild of image layers, bypassing cache.\n\ndocker images\n\ud83d\udc49 List all container images stored locally on your system.\n\ndocker rmi image_id\n\ud83d\udc49 Deletes a local image to free disk space.\n\ndocker tag source_tag target_tag\n\ud83d\udc49 Creates an alias tag referencing a target image.\n\ndocker history image_name\n\ud83d\udc49 Shows the list of filesystem layers in an image.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.3
    },
    {
      "id": "rBoWC6cbshuyG2M8hax9M",
